CM_ BO_ 2 "Steering angle sensor. Our testing confirmed steering-angle behavior, steering-rate behavior, fixed 0x07 field, approximately 100 Hz transmission, and 4-bit rolling counter.";
CM_ BO_ 361 "Existing Nissan LKAS definition. Passive recording cabana_data.csv contains 149340 instances of 0x169, half each on bus 0 and bus 2. Presence and DLC=8 confirmed; signal meanings and command acceptance not independently verified by this recording. Do not infer transmit permissions or actuation.";
CM_ SG_ 634 SET_0x4D "Observed constant 0x4D in prior recording; not an instruction to transmit.";
CM_ SG_ 634 COUNTER_27A "Confirmed 4-bit rolling counter in byte 6 low nibble. Sequence 0 through 15 then wraps to 0.";
CM_ SG_ 634 CHECKSUM_27A "Confirmed additive checksum. Checksum = (Byte1 + Byte2 + Byte3 + Byte4 + Byte5 + Byte6 + 0x7C) & 0xFF.";
CM_ BO_ 943 "Observed hazard switch input indication; pulses were followed by reported hazard-lamp activity. This does not establish a CAN actuator command or external transmit permission.";
CM_ BO_ 1549 "Door-status message also contains turn-signal state. Captured on BUS 0 at 10.3 Hz. Byte 2 toggles 0x06 <-> 0x66 in lockstep with the 0x27A flash, which confirms bits 5 and 6 as the two blinker lamps. Like 0x27A this message REPORTS lamp state.";

CM_ BO_ 460 "Observed 4-byte payload on buses 0 and 2. Raw BRAKE_PEDAL-named field changes during manual AND factory automatic braking; not a driver-only pedal measurement; units uncalibrated. Receive-only.";
CM_ BO_ 451 "Observed on Panda bus 1, 8-byte payload approximately 100 Hz during one drive; six factory-braking-associated episodes. Existing BRAKE_PRESSURE (raw uncalibrated magnitude) and BRAKE_ACTIVE change during episodes. Byte6 bits0-1 form modulo-4 counter; Byte6 bit2 is additional brake-correlated state; Byte8 is an additive integrity byte matched in 263475/263475 captured frames. ECU transmitter, request vs feedback, physical units, and actuation capability remain UNVERIFIED. RECEIVE/DECODE ONLY.";
CM_ BO_ 861 "Passive observations: eight-byte 0x35D on buses 0 and 2. Byte 5 bit 4 associated with brake-pedal state (about 98 percent when BRAKE_PEDAL at least 10 in sampled test window). No actuation meaning established.";
CM_ SG_ 634 OBS_BRAKE_CORRELATED_B4_BIT5 "Passive association with brake presses in Nov 2026 Park test; does not imply the 0x27A turn-signal status message controls braking.";
CM_ SG_ 852 OBS_BRAKE_CORRELATED_B7_BIT4 "Passive association with brake presses in Nov 2026 Park test. Correlation only; not proven brake-switch or control signal.";
CM_ SG_ 861 OBS_BRAKE_CORRELATED_B5_BIT4 "Passive association with brake presses in Nov 2026 Park test. Correlation only; not proven brake-switch or control signal.";
CM_ BO_ 634 "Turn-signal and brake-correlated status observations share the same CAN payload. This message was observed on bus 0 and 2 in the Nov 2026 recording. Its fields are state/observation definitions, NOT validated actuation commands.";
CM_ SG_ 451 BRAKE_PRESSURE "Existing 9-bit field, raw scale 1; 0-364 observed in recorded factory brake events; physical pressure units and request-vs-feedback meaning not verified.";
CM_ SG_ 451 BRAKE_ACTIVE "Existing one-bit field, observed asserted with nonzero magnitude during factory braking; not proof this bit commands the brakes.";
CM_ SG_ 451 OBS_BRAKE_STATE_B6_BIT2 "Byte 6 bit 2. Observed asserted in 3586 frames, including 621 without brake-active bit; state meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 451 OBS_COUNTER_B6_BITS0_1 "Byte 6 low two bits cycle 0,1,2,3; 99.998 percent of transitions consistent with rolling count. Receive-side observation only.";
CM_ SG_ 451 OBS_CHECKSUM_B8 "Last-byte additive integrity relationship observed in all 263475 raw frames. Not a validated transmission interface.";
CM_ BO_ 654 "New read-only definition for CAN ID 0x28E on Panda bus 1; DLC 6. Byte 3 bit 0 was asserted in about 97.1 percent of factory-braking-active 0.2-second bins and 0 percent inactive bins in one analysis window. Correlation, not identified control.";
CM_ BO_ 761 "New read-only definition for CAN ID 0x2F9 on buses 0 and 2; DLC 2. Byte 1 bit 6 mostly CLEARS during factory-braking-active intervals (5.4 percent active vs 98.3 percent inactive). Correlation, not identified control.";
CM_ SG_ 459 OBS_AUTO_BRAKE_ASSOC_B2_BIT5 "Byte 2 bit 5: 81.8 percent braking-active vs 4.5 percent inactive sampled bins; tentative association only.";
CM_ SG_ 682 OBS_AUTO_BRAKE_ASSOC_B3_BIT5 "Byte 3 bit 5: 97.1 percent braking-active vs 0 percent inactive sampled bins. Tentative state, not request.";
CM_ SG_ 688 OBS_AUTO_BRAKE_ASSOC_B3_BIT6 "Byte 3 bit 6: 94.6 percent braking-active vs 1.7 percent inactive sampled bins. Tentative state, not request.";
CM_ SG_ 654 OBS_AUTO_BRAKE_ASSOC_B3_BIT0 "Byte 3 bit 0: 97.1 percent braking-active vs 0 percent inactive sampled bins. Tentative state, not request.";
CM_ SG_ 761 OBS_AUTO_BRAKE_INVERSE_B1_BIT6 "Byte 1 bit 6: 5.4 percent braking-active vs 98.3 percent inactive sampled bins; inverse association, unknown physical meaning.";
CM_ BO_ 569 "Existing cruise and pedal-related definitions. USER_BRAKE_PRESSED remained 0 in sampled factory-automatic-braking intervals, useful distinction from BRAKE_PEDAL-named 0x1CC field. Check per model-year before safety-critical use.";
CM_ BO_ 682 "Observed on buses 0 and 2, 8 bytes. Existing raw-byte observations retained; Byte 3 bit 5 tracks factory brake episodes; magnitude in Bytes 1-2 strongly correlated with 0x1C3 (r about 0.998 during braking intervals), but signal boundaries, source, units and request-vs-feedback remain unknown. Receive-only.";
CM_ BO_ 688 "Observed on bus 1, 8 bytes. Existing raw-byte observations retained; Byte 3 bit 6 tracks factory brake episodes. Source, meaning and request-vs-feedback unknown. Receive-only.";
